sysreseval (0.20.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sre-web portal: shared projects. The owner of a running project shares it
    with everybody or with one of their groups; a student asks to join from
    "Open a shared lab…" of the Open page and the owner accepts; a participant
    works in the same terminals, answers, states, virtual desktop and
    self-evaluation (closing and saving stay the owner's). [sharing] of
    web.toml, "no-by-default" by default: nothing is shared until an instructor
    allows the project. Exam, GUI, debug and instructor-mode projects are never
    shared. The portal and every agent must be restarted together: an older
    agent refuses participants
  * sre-web portal: the Watch page gets a Sharing column and a selection with
    bulk actions (allow, forbid or default sharing, close projects)
  * sre-web portal: saved projects work again after a reboot of the pool hosts
    (the check now mounts the automounted volume; every host but one was flagged
    "saves unusable")
  * make-web-hosts.sh: ROOM_PRIORITIES and ROOM_USABLE_CAPACITIES accept a
    single machine as well as a room (ROOM_PRIORITIES="a=50 a3=35 b=10")
  * Docker images 1.36 (proxy13 and devops13 1.37): the images built on Debian
    13 take a 13 suffix and are merged by machine role, 16 → 11: netdev13 (FRR,
    multicast, lldpd, stayrtr, Open vSwitch / OS-Ken, chrony), identity13 (LDAP,
    mail, FreeRADIUS, 802.1X, Kerberos), devops13 (docker-ce 29, Vagrant,
    Ansible, k3s), proxy13 (+ Squid 6, squidGuard), new nsm13 (Zeek 9.0, Cowrie
    3.1.8). A lab naming a former image still starts (its last tag, 1.35)
  * init12 / init13 images: the systemd of a privileged machine no longer acts
    on the host (udev replay of every host device, kernel.core_pattern, getty on
    tty1, power keys), seen as crashes of the camera service of a logged-in user
    at the start of the dhcp lab
  * changes in drafts labs

 -- emotchane <emmanuel.motchane@gmail.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:59:21 +0100

sysreseval (0.19.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sre-web portal: saved projects. A user saves a running project (labs with
    allow_save_restore) into a directory shared by the pool hosts, restores it
    later on any host and shares it with groups; a Saved projects page, a limit
    per user ([saves] of web.toml and agent.toml, off by default); a host that
    cannot use the directory is flagged "saves unusable" on the Pool page and by
    sre-web-tool list, with the reason * sre-web portal: the Archives page shows
    the content of an archive file (as sre cat does) and downloads it
    ([archives] directory of web.toml) * sre save / restore: a project restored
    from a save and saved again restores on any host (updated Kathara fork, in
    python3-kathara; a checkout runs make venv again) * question hashes come
    from the default language of the lab only: adding or correcting a
    translation no longer detaches the stored answers (answers under the former
    hash are still graded); new command pin-question-hashes (sbin/ of a
    checkout, /usr/bin of the package) writes hash= on every question of a lab *
    lab tree: "@subtitle..." keys in a titles.json in manual order group the
    labs under subtitles (Open dialog of the GUI, Open page of the web site);
    the _DRAFT_misc labs grouped under ten topics
  * various new draft labs and fixes

 -- emotchane <emmanuel.motchane@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:39:54 +0100

